*"Who can trade" comes straight out of each platform's own terms. It's a fact about
their rules, not advice, and definitely not a workaround. Hover a cell to see the
countries by name, click it for the document I read them from. 🌐 permissionless means
the protocol enforces nothing, though the official front end may still block you.*

*Volume is notional USD over the period shown. A blank means nobody publishes a free
comparable figure, and the entry says what turned up instead. Some venues disclose only
commission revenue or a contract count. Neither of those is volume.*

***Don't add the column up.*** *Brokers route their flow into exchanges sitting in the
same table, so you'd count it twice. Dead venues keep their file in [`data/`](data/) but
drop off the page.*

